  "id": "COMPOUND:757 - PROTEIN:5362",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism linking etoposide to Ca-Ski through a series of molecular interactions involving palmarumycin CP18. Etoposide, a well-established chemotherapeutic agent, is directly linked to Ubiquitin carboxyl-terminal hydrolase 5 and P2X purinoceptor 7, both of which are targets of palmarumycin CP18. This compound then acts as a bridge to Ca-Ski, indicating a possible pathway where palmarumycin CP18 modulates the activity of these targets to influence Ca-Ski. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a robust, albeit indirect, relationship between etoposide and Ca-Ski, mediated by palmarumycin CP18. The mechanism involves a cascade of interactions that may regulate cellular processes through the modulation of these targets. The presence of a well-documented mode of action through palmarumycin CP18 supports the hypothesis, though the exact functional role of each intermediate step remains to be fully elucidated.",
